                                        <h6 class="mb-3">

NISM Series IV Interest rate Derivatives and NISM IV Question Bank details

</h6>
										
                                        <div class="mb-4">
                                            <p>

The NISM Series 4 – Interest Rate Derivatives Certification Exam stands out as a pivotal certification within the NISM portfolio, offering invaluable insights into Fixed Income Securities and Interest Rate Derivative products. This certification holds paramount importance in providing professionals with a comprehensive understanding of the intricate workings of these financial instruments. By delving into the complexities of interest rate derivatives, candidates gain a nuanced perspective on managing risk, optimizing portfolios, and navigating dynamic market environments. Furthermore, mastering this certification empowers individuals to make informed decisions, thereby contributing to enhanced financial stability and proficiency in the realm of fixed income securities and interest rate derivatives.
</p>
                                            
                                        </div>
                                        
                                       
                                       
                                        
										<h6 class="mb-3">Examination Objectives</h6>
										<p>The objectives of the NISM Series 4 – Interest Rate Derivatives Certification Exam include:</p>
										 <ul class="car-single-list">
                                                <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i>Comprehensive Understanding: To provide candidates with a comprehensive understanding of interest rate derivative products, including their features, characteristics, and applications in financial markets.</li>
                                                <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i> Risk Management Proficiency: To equip candidates with the knowledge and skills necessary to effectively manage risks associated with interest rate derivatives, including hedging strategies, risk measurement techniques, and risk mitigation approaches.</li>
                                                <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i>Regulatory Compliance: To ensure candidates have a clear understanding of the regulatory framework governing interest rate derivatives markets, including relevant laws, regulations, and guidelines issued by regulatory authorities.</li>
											 <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i>Application in Financial Decision Making: To enable candidates to apply their knowledge of interest rate derivatives in real-world financial scenarios, including portfolio management, trading strategies, and investment decision-making processes.</li>
											 <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i>Enhancing Market Integrity: To contribute to the integrity and efficiency of financial markets by promoting well-informed and knowledgeable professionals who can participate responsibly in interest rate derivatives trading and related activities.</li>
                                               
                                            </ul>
										<h6 class="mb-3">Assessment Structure</h6>
                                        


										<p>The (NISM Series 4: Interest rate Derivatives Examination) will have a total of 100 marks, with 100 questions, each carrying a weight of 1 mark. Candidates are allotted 2 hours to complete the exam. Negative marking of 25% of the marks assigned to each question will be applied for incorrect answers. The passing score for the examination is set at 60%.
</p><br>
